<section class="page-head section section--tight">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="figure-note">Last updated <time datetime="{{ updated }}">{{ updated }}</time></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">
        The short version: this site doesn't track you. There are no ads, no analytics, no
        cookies, and no accounts. It's a set of static pages and nothing you do here is sent
        to us or stored.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing automatically. This site has no analytics, no tracking pixels, no cookies, and no
        contact forms, and it doesn't store anything in your browser.
      </p>
      <p>
        The directory's &ldquo;Suggest a doctor&rdquo; and &ldquo;Report outdated info&rdquo; links
        open your own email app with a pre-filled message. Nothing is sent unless you choose to send
        it. If you do, we receive your email address and whatever you write. We use it only to check
        and update the directory and, if needed, to reply to you. We never publish your name or email
        address, and we don't sell or share it. Please don't include health details you don't need
        to. Emails are handled by our email provider (Microsoft Outlook) under its own privacy terms,
        and we delete a message on request.
      </p>

      <h2>2. The self-check</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/diagnosis.html">self-check</a> runs entirely in your browser. Your answers
        and result never leave your device and are not saved &mdash; refreshing the page clears them.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Clinicians listed in the directory</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href="/find-a-doctor.html">doctor directory</a> shows clinicians' names and
        professional details: clinic, work address, work phone number, and profile page. This comes
        from patient reports and from information clinicians or their employers have published. We
        show it so people with RCPD can find care, and we don't publish anyone's personal (non-work)
        contact details. Clinicians can ask us to correct or remove their listing at
        <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub may automatically process
        basic technical information (such as your IP address) in its server logs to deliver the
        site and protect against abuse. We don't have access to those logs. That processing is
        governed by
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>5. External links</h2>
      <p>
        This site links to outside resources &mdash; research papers, videos, doctors' websites,
        and the r/noburp community. We aren't responsible for their content or privacy practices;
        please review their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Your rights &amp; contact</h2>
      <p>
        Laws such as Canada's PIPEDA, the EU/UK GDPR, and the California Consumer Privacy Act give
        you rights over your personal data. For this site, that personal data is limited to emails
        you send us and, for clinicians, directory listings. You can ask us to access, correct, or
        delete that information, or ask a privacy question, by emailing
        <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. We don't sell or share personal
        data, and we don't use it for advertising. If we ever add something that processes personal
        data &mdash; for example, analytics &mdash; we will update this policy first and describe
        your choices.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This site is a general-audience educational resource and is not directed at children. We do
        not knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date above will change with it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
